er of consecutive loan renewals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate item eligibility within 2 seconds and issue the loan receipt\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes only the happy-path eligibility validation and receipt issuance without specifying system behavior when an item is ineligible or validation fails.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the allowed maximum number of active hold requests\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"References a cap on active hold requests without specifying the actual numeric limit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"borrow up to 8 physical items simultaneously\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-009\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Allows a Member to borrow up to 8 physical items simultaneously, contradicting SD-009 which caps checked-out physical items at 5.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-016\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"21 calendar days from the checkout timestamp\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Sets the standard loan period for circulating print books to 21 calendar days, contradicting SD-010 which specifies 14 calendar days.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-017\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"self-register online with only an email address and immediately check out physical books without Librarian ID verification\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-001\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Permits unverified self-registration with only an email address and immediate book checkout without ID verification, contradicting SD-001 which requires a Librarian to verify government-issued photo ID and record full name, email address, and phone number.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-018\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"remain held indefinitely until the requesting Member explicitly cancels the hold\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-011\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"States that reserved items on the pickup shelf remain held indefinitely until cancelled by the Member, contradicting SD-011 which cancels uncollected holds after 72 hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-021\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"coordination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"send an overdue email and/or suspend borrowing privileges and/or apply a penalty flag\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses stacked \\\"and/or\\\" connectives, leaving it ambiguous which combination of actions is mandatory when an item becomes 7 days overdue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall be reviewed, approved, and recorded\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without specifying which role or system component reviews, approves, and records overdue fine waiver requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the subjective loophole qualifier \\\"if appropriate\\\", making SMS due-date alert dispatch optional and untestable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD years\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved \\\"TBD\\\" placeholder for the payment receipt retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-025\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"$1.25 USD per overdue day per item with no maximum cap\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-019\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Assesses an overdue fine of $1.25 USD per day with no cap, contradicting SD-019 which sets the fine at $0.50 USD per overdue day capped at $20.00 USD per item.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-026\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"renew borrowed items online at any time regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-020\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Allows a Member to renew borrowed items regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance, contradicting SD-020 which blocks Members with unpaid fines exceeding $5.00 USD from renewing items.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-027\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Patron\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-001\", \"SD-009\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Introduces the term \\\"Patron\\\" for the borrower entity referred to as \\\"Member\\\" in earlier requirements (beginning in SD-001 and in SD-009 for the 5-item borrowing limit).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"quickly; many users\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses unquantified terms (\\\"quickly\\\", \\\"many users\\\") without defining measurable latency or concurrency thresholds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"where possible\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the non-binding qualifier \\\"where possible\\\", making query-term highlighting in result snippets optional and unverifiable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-030\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"sufficient; acceptable\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective, unquantified terms (\\\"sufficient\\\", \\\"acceptable\\\") instead of measurable ISBN matching accuracy and response-time targets.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-031\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"efficiently; large; noticeable\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses vague, unquantified terms (\\\"efficiently\\\", \\\"large\\\", \\\"noticeable\\\") without specifying batch size, throughput, or acceptable system degradation limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall detect the active references\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies detecting active loans or holds when a Librarian attempts to delete a bibliographic record, but omits the resulting system action (such as blocking deletion and returning an error).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-034\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD intervals\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved \\\"TBD\\\" placeholder for the full database backup interval.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-035\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"important; in a timely manner; an appropriate period\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses vague, unquantified terms (\\\"important\\\", \\\"in a timely manner\\\", \\\"an appropriate period\\\") without defining which administrative actions are audited, logging latency, or retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-036\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall log event FAILOVER-01\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies only logging event FAILOVER-01 when the primary database node is unreachable for more than 10 seconds, omitting the actual failover, traffic redirection, or recovery behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-037\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"adequate; clear\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective, unquantified terms (\\\"adequate\\\", \\\"clear\\\") instead of specifying concrete transport security standards and authentication error-message criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-038\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"accept any Member password of at least 8 characters\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-002\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Accepts any Member password of at least 8 characters, contradicting SD-002 which requires at least 12 characters containing uppercase, lowercase, and numeric characters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-039\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"60 minutes of user inactivity\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"SD-004\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Keeps authenticated web portal sessions active for 60 minutes of inactivity, contradicting SD-004 which terminates sessions after 15 minutes of inactivity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-040\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"encrypt all Member passwords using reversible AES-256 encryption so Administrators can decrypt and retrieve forgotten passwords\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\"S